{"name":"Vault-Tec Yellow","hex":"#efcc5b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vault","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An arched masonry structure supporting and forming a ceiling, whether freestanding or forming part of a larger building.","Any arched ceiling or roof."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build as, or cover with a vault.","To store in a vault."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vault"},{"term":"tec","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Terik."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of 'tec (“detective”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tec"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vault-Tec","blocks":[{"text":"Vault-Tec Corporation, otherwise known as Vault-Tec and sometimes called Vault-Tec Industries, is a fictional defense megacorporation from the post-apocalyptic Fallout franchise. Throughout the United States, Vault-Tec created government-funded vaults, large fallout shelters that would serve to shelter civilians and allow for the continuation of human life in the threat of a nuclear attack. Within most of these Overseer-governed vaults, Vault-Tec carried out human experiments on its residents without their consent or knowledge, ranging from being mostly harmless to disturbing and inhumane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Vault-Tec_Corporation_logo.svg/330px-Vault-Tec_Corporation_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vault-Tec"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Fallout_4_at_Gamescom_2015_%2820402858326%29.jpg/500px-Fallout_4_at_Gamescom_2015_%2820402858326%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Fallout_4_at_Gamescom_2015_%2820402858326%29.jpg/1280px-Fallout_4_at_Gamescom_2015_%2820402858326%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Fallout_4_at_Gamescom_2015_%2820402858326%29.jpg/500px-Fallout_4_at_Gamescom_2015_%2820402858326%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Vault-Tec themed van at Gamescom 2015","l